<title>CANADA: CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacant space in Canadian Prairie primary elevators rose to 35 percent in the week ended June 15 while railcar unloads fell short of target levels, Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>The 35 percent average vacancy in Prairie elevators was up from 33 percent on June 8, the Board said.</p>
<p>Manitoba had the most space at 39 percent followed by Alberta at 37 percent then Saskatchewan at 29 percent.</p>
<p>Vancouver unloaded 3,124 railcars versus the 3,300 target. Prince Rupert unloaded 1,167 railcars versus the 1,300 target. Thunder Bay unloaded 3,354 railcars versus the 3,220 target.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
